<title>CANADA: Canada lumber union pickets Greenpeace.</title>
<headline>Canada lumber union pickets Greenpeace.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The union representing British Columbia's lumber workers picketed the environmental group Greenpeace on Monday, the union said.</p>
<p>The picketing began on Saturday on the Vancouver docks where the Greenpeace vessel Arctic Sunrise was tied up. A union spokesman said between four and 20 members were taking part in the picketing at any given time.</p>
<p>The IWA-Canada union said it was protesting the environmental group's campaign aimed at convincing consumers to boycott the province's forest products. Greenpeace claims logging practices in the province are damaging and unsustainable.</p>
<p>&quot;Our members are fed up with the antics of Greenpeace and we are just giving them a taste of their own medicine. This organization...should get out of British Columbia altogether,&quot; said union official Brian Harder.</p>
<p>((Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314))</p>
